STEP 1 — DELETE APPLICATION NAMESPACE

Delete ALL application resources:

kubectl delete namespace vk67220-ns

Verify:

kubectl get ns

Wait until:

vk67220-ns

disappears.

STEP 2 — DELETE ARGOCD APPLICATION
kubectl delete application employee-project -n argocd
STEP 3 — DELETE ARGOCD

If installed using Helm:

helm uninstall argocd -n argocd

Then:

kubectl delete namespace argocd
STEP 4 — DELETE INGRESS CONTROLLER

VERY IMPORTANT.

Otherwise AWS ELB billing continues.

kubectl delete namespace ingress-nginx

Verify:

kubectl get svc -A

No LoadBalancer services should remain.

STEP 5 — DELETE CERT-MANAGER
kubectl delete namespace cert-manager
STEP 6 — DELETE METRICS SERVER
helm uninstall metrics-server -n kube-system
STEP 7 — VERIFY LOADBALANCERS REMOVED

Go AWS Console:

EC2 →
Load Balancers.

Ensure:
❌ no ELBs remain.

OR CLI:

aws elbv2 describe-load-balancers
STEP 8 — DELETE EKS NODEGROUP

List nodegroups:

aws eks list-nodegroups \
--cluster-name <cluster-name> \
--region us-east-1

Delete:

aws eks delete-nodegroup \
--cluster-name <cluster-name> \
--nodegroup-name <nodegroup-name> \
--region us-east-1

Wait until deleted.

STEP 9 — DELETE EKS CLUSTER
aws eks delete-cluster \
--name <cluster-name> \
--region us-east-1
STEP 10 — VERIFY CLUSTER DELETED
aws eks list-clusters --region us-east-1
STEP 11 — DELETE EBS VOLUMES

VERY IMPORTANT.

EBS volumes often remain.

AWS Console:
EC2 →
Volumes.

Delete all:

Available
Kubernetes leftover volumes.

OR CLI:

aws ec2 describe-volumes

Delete:

aws ec2 delete-volume --volume-id vol-xxxxxxxx
STEP 12 — DELETE ECR IMAGES

List repositories:

aws ecr describe-repositories

Delete repository:

aws ecr delete-repository \
--repository-name employees-app-dev \
--force
STEP 13 — DELETE SECURITY GROUPS (OPTIONAL)

Sometimes EKS leaves:

SGs
ENIs.

Check AWS Console.

STEP 14 — VERIFY BILLING RESOURCES

Most important final checks:

AWS Service	Must be Empty
EC2	no worker nodes
EKS	no cluster
ELB	no load balancer
EBS	no leftover volumes
ECR	optional
NAT Gateway	delete if exists
MOST IMPORTANT BILLING RESOURCES

These cost the MOST:

Resource	Billing
NAT Gateway	VERY expensive
LoadBalancer	hourly
EBS	monthly
EC2 nodes	hourly
Elastic IP	if unattached
VERIFY NAT GATEWAY

Go:
VPC →
NAT Gateways.

Delete if exists.

VERY IMPORTANT.

FINAL AWS CLEANUP CHECKLIST

✅ Namespace deleted
✅ ArgoCD deleted
✅ ingress-nginx deleted
✅ cert-manager deleted
✅ metrics-server deleted
✅ ELBs deleted
✅ nodegroups deleted
✅ EKS cluster deleted
✅ EBS volumes deleted
✅ NAT gateways deleted
✅ ECR cleaned.
